# Project Context

This repo serves **quantum-information-expertise.com**, a Jekyll/minima site hosted on GitHub Pages (pja35.github.io) for Pablo Arrighi's independent consulting activity. I also has Pablo Arrighi's CV.

## Who

Pablo Arrighi — Senior Researcher (DR) at Inria, specializing in quantum computing, quantum simulation, and quantum gravity. Key credentials:
- Author of "A typology of quantum algorithms" and 60+ publications
- Former member of CoNRS Section 6 (CNRS national evaluation committee)
- Referee for national research funding agencies (ANR, etc.)
- Operates a micro-entreprise under French law for consulting

## Goal

Offer independent scientific due diligence and advisory services (up to ~1 day/week) to:
- Quantum technology investment funds
- Scientific advisory boards of startups
- Banks and corporate innovation teams
- Expert networks (AlphaSights, etc.)

Target platforms for visibility: AlphaSights, Toptal, Upwork.

## Repo Structure

- `_config.yml`, `Gemfile` — Jekyll config (theme: minima, domain: quantum-information-expertise.com)
- `index.md`, `advisory.md`, `expertise.md`, `contact.md` — site content pages
- `_includes/header.html`, `_includes/footer.html` — custom layout partials
- `assets/` — SCSS styles, logo, email image
- `REFS/CV-Arrighi.pdf` — academic CV (PDF)
- `REFS/CV-Arrighi/word/document.xml` — academic CV (uncompressed docx XML)

## Two Main Tasks

1. **Adapt the CV** from academic format to a consulting-oriented format suitable for expert networks and freelance platforms
2. **Build/refine the website** at quantum-information-expertise.com as a professional landing page for the consulting activity
